Popular Generative AI Tools for DevOps
 1. Coding & Scripting Assistants

GitHub Copilot / Amazon CodeWhisperer / Tabnine → AI pair programmers that help generate code, CI/CD YAML, Terraform, Ansible, and Kubernetes manifests.

Ansible Lightspeed (IBM + Red Hat) → AI-assisted Ansible playbook generation.

Pulumi AI → Generates Infrastructure as Code (IaC) in multiple languages.

 2. CI/CD & Release Automation with AI

Harness.io → AI-driven Continuous Delivery (predicts failures, automates rollbacks).

Jenkins with AI plugins → Uses AI to recommend pipeline optimizations and test coverage.

GitLab Duo → AI assistant inside GitLab for pipelines, code reviews, and security fixes.

3. Monitoring, AIOps & Troubleshooting

Dynatrace Davis AI → Predicts outages (e.g., memory leaks, latency spikes).

Datadog AIOps → AI-based anomaly detection and incident triage.

New Relic AI → Correlates logs/metrics with AI to cut down alert noise.

Google Cloud AIOps / AWS DevOps Guru / Azure Monitor AI → Cloud-native predictive monitoring.

4. Kubernetes & CloudOps AI Tools

Kubiya.ai → AI-powered DevOps virtual assistant for K8s and cloud workflows.

StormForge → Uses ML to optimize Kubernetes workloads (cost & performance).

BotKube + LLMs → ChatOps for Kubernetes (query cluster status in plain English).

KubeGPT → Conversational AI for K8s troubleshooting.

 5. DevSecOps with AI

Snyk AI → Fixes vulnerabilities with AI code suggestions.

GitHub Advanced Security + Copilot → Detects secrets, misconfigs, vulnerabilities.

Aqua Security Trivy AI → AI-based container and supply-chain scanning.

 6. Knowledge & Incident Management

PagerDuty AI Ops → Groups alerts, predicts incident causes, and suggests fixes.

FireHydrant / Shoreline AI Runbooks → Auto-generate remediation steps.

Slack GPT / MS Teams Copilot → AI-driven ChatOps assistants for DevOps teams.

Summary:

Generative AI is reshaping DevOps by:

Automating code & IaC creation (Copilot, Pulumi AI, Ansible Lightspeed)

Making CI/CD smarter (Harness, GitLab Duo)

Predicting failures before they happen (Dynatrace, DevOps Guru)

Optimizing Kubernetes & cloud costs (StormForge, Kubiya.ai)

Strengthening security (Snyk AI, Aqua Security)

Improving incident response (PagerDuty AI, FireHydrant)
